{"name":"Noxious","hex":"#89a203","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"noxious","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Harmful; injurious.","Morally corrupting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noxious"}],"entries":[{"title":"Poison","blocks":[{"text":"In science, a poison is any chemical substance that is harmful or lethal to a living organism. The term of poison is used in a wide range of scientific fields and industries, where it is often specifically defined. It may also be applied colloquially or figuratively, with a broad sense."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/GHS-pictogram-skull.svg/330px-GHS-pictogram-skull.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poison","wikidata":"Q40867"},{"title":"Noxious weed","blocks":[{"text":"A noxious weed, harmful weed or injurious weed is a weed that has been designated by an agricultural or other governing authority as a plant that is harmful to agricultural or horticultural crops, natural habitats or ecosystems, or humans or livestock. Most noxious weeds have been introduced into an ecosystem by ignorance, mismanagement, or accident. Some noxious weeds are native, though many localities define them as necessarily being non-native. Typically, they are plants that grow aggressively, multiply quickly without natural controls, and cause adverse effects upon contact or ingestion. Noxious weeds are a major problem in many parts of the world, greatly affecting areas of agriculture, forest management, nature reserves, parks, and other open spaces."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Cotton_Thistle%2C_Galong%2C_New_South_Wales.jpg/330px-Cotton_Thistle%2C_Galong%2C_New_South_Wales.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noxious_weed","wikidata":"Q7067310"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Saka-saka_-_cassava_leaves_in_mortar_and_pestle.jpg/500px-Saka-saka_-_cassava_leaves_in_mortar_and_pestle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Saka-saka_-_cassava_leaves_in_mortar_and_pestle.jpg/500px-Saka-saka_-_cassava_leaves_in_mortar_and_pestle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cassava leaves contain cyanide and can thus cause poisoning if not prepared correctly.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaka-saka_-_cassava_leaves_in_mortar_and_pestle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Lagoa_vermelha_na_Mina_do_Losal_05.jpg/500px-Lagoa_vermelha_na_Mina_do_Losal_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Lagoa_vermelha_na_Mina_do_Losal_05.jpg/500px-Lagoa_vermelha_na_Mina_do_Losal_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Polluted groundwater, in this case depicting acid mine drainage, can cause chronic poisoning.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALagoa_vermelha_na_Mina_do_Losal_05.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Jan_Matejko-Poisoning_of_Queen_Bona.jpg/500px-Jan_Matejko-Poisoning_of_Queen_Bona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Jan_Matejko-Poisoning_of_Queen_Bona.jpg/1280px-Jan_Matejko-Poisoning_of_Queen_Bona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Jan_Matejko-Poisoning_of_Queen_Bona.jpg/500px-Jan_Matejko-Poisoning_of_Queen_Bona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Poisoning of Queen Bona by Jan Matejko.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJan_Matejko-Poisoning_of_Queen_Bona.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/CaulerpaTaxifolia.jpg/500px-CaulerpaTaxifolia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/CaulerpaTaxifolia.jpg/500px-CaulerpaTaxifolia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The alga Caulerpa taxifolia is a noxious marine weed nicknamed killer algae. This is a picture of it invading a native plant bed.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACaulerpaTaxifolia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Striga_gesnerioides_-_Purple_Witchweed_%285039468678%29.jpg/500px-Striga_gesnerioides_-_Purple_Witchweed_%285039468678%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Striga_gesnerioides_-_Purple_Witchweed_%285039468678%29.jpg/500px-Striga_gesnerioides_-_Purple_Witchweed_%285039468678%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This is a parasitic noxious weed, Striga gesnerioides, the cowpea witchweed.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStriga_gesnerioides_-_Purple_Witchweed_(5039468678).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Drymaria_arenarioides_90650942.jpg/500px-Drymaria_arenarioides_90650942.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Drymaria_arenarioides_90650942.jpg/1280px-Drymaria_arenarioides_90650942.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Drymaria_arenarioides_90650942.jpg/500px-Drymaria_arenarioides_90650942.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe